  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 116 AM CDT Thu Oct 15 2026\n\nMid-upper level trough that has been supplying the area with\ndreary weather conditions will depart later this morning and\ninto this afternoon. Any lingering rain, storms, and fog will\ndiminish from southwest to northeast late this morning with\nclearing skies and breezy conditions into the later afternoon.\nTonight has the potential to bring some frost and perhaps a\nfreeze. However, uncertainty remains with the level of winds \nthat could limit those impacts, so held off on any headlines for\nnow.\n\nFrost/Freeze headlines will be near certain Friday night into\nSaturday morning as widespread upper 20s to low 30s are expected\nacross nearly all of western and central Kansas. With light\nwinds and clear skies, freeze and frost are highly likely. This\nis shaping up to be a widespread issue for plants, so\nprecautions should be started to protect any most vulnerable\ncrops and plants. A warming trend will commence for the latter\nhalf of the weekend and into next week as 850 mb temperature\nanomalies go back to above average per global models. As far as\nthe next chance of any precipitation is concerned, only low POPs\n(30-40%) are in the forecast Wednesday and Thursday, but varying\npatterns are evident among the globals, putting low confidence \nin the longer range.",
